# Branch protection + pull request workflow

This repo has branch protection on `main`. Follow these rules whenever making changes.

## Always work on a branch (never directly on main)
- Do not commit directly to `main`.
- Create a feature branch from `main` for every change.
- Use short, descriptive branch names, e.g. `feat/nsrdb-client`, `chore/repo-structure`, `fix/timezone-join`.

## Commit discipline
- Use Conventional Commits (e.g. `feat: ...`, `fix: ...`, `docs: ...`, `chore: ...`).
- Keep commits focused and small enough to review.

## Pull request requirements
- Open a PR from your feature branch into `main`.
- PR description must include:
  - what changed and why (1–3 bullets)
  - how to run/verify (test plan)
  - any risks or follow-ups
- If checks are present (lint/tests), they must pass before merging.

## Merge strategy
- Prefer squash-merge for a clean history unless there’s a reason to preserve commit structure.
- Delete the feature branch after merge.

